# Local-only values for your custom-code functions. NEVER committed
# (this directory's .gitignore excludes .env).
#
# Setup:
#   cp .env.example .env
#   # then edit .env with real values
#
# Keys here must match the env var names declared in secrets.yaml.
# In production, these values come from the Cresta secret manager;
# this file is only used by `cresta custom-code serve` for local development.
#
# Precedence: a variable already exported in the environment that starts
# `cresta custom-code serve` overrides the value set here, so a tool that
# injects a rotated secret is not undone by a stale entry in this file.
# Entries with no exported counterpart load normally.
#
# Once .env is populated, you can push values to the server in one shot:
#   cresta secret push
#
# Example (uncomment and edit):
# MY_API_KEY=local-dev-key-here
